= Introduction <ch:introduction>

== Purpose of the Report

The Estates Committee approved a one-year bike-share pilot in March 2024 and asked the Transport Working Group
to report on it before deciding whether to fund the scheme permanently. This report is that evaluation. It is
written for committee members who have not followed the pilot closely, so each chapter can be read on its own.

== The Pilot in Brief

The scheme placed 120 bicycles at ten docking stations: six on the main campus, three on the science campus
1.8 km away, and one at the railway station. Staff and students unlocked a bicycle with their university
card. The first thirty minutes of each trip were free, which covers a ride between any two stations.

Schemes of this kind are now common in cities and on campuses, and their effects have been studied widely
@shaheen2010bikesharing @fishman2013bike. The pilot was designed with that experience in mind, in particular
the finding that stations must be close together for a scheme to be used.

== Goals Set by the Committee <sec:goals>

The committee set three goals, and asked that each be judged with a measure agreed in advance:

+ *Use.* At least 40,000 trips in the year.
+ *Cost.* A lower cost per trip than the inter-campus shuttle bus.
+ *Car travel.* A measurable reduction in car journeys between the two campuses.

== Structure of the Report

@ch:methods explains where the figures come from. @ch:results presents the results against each goal, and
@ch:recommendations gives our recommendations and the risks we see.
